# Pin line endings so the two machines this project is worked on from agree.
#
# Without this, behaviour depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, which is a local setting that
# never travels with a clone. A machine set to `true` checks files out as CRLF while one set to
# `input` or `false` leaves them LF, and the difference shows up as whole-file phantom diffs that
# bury the real change.
#
# text=auto lets Git decide what is text rather than listing extensions; eol=lf keeps the working
# tree LF to match what is already stored, which also silences the "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warnings that appear when an editor writes LF into a CRLF working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe requires CRLF, and mvnw.cmd is executable.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Binary, so Git must never touch the bytes.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
